<p>Warner Bros Discovery shareholders voted on Thursday to approve Paramount’s takeover of the company, bringing one of the biggest recent media deals a step closer to completion. Across the coverage, the transaction is valued at about $110 billion or $111 billion including debt, and reports said shareholders were offered $31 a share. The vote gives a key corporate green light to the proposed combination of Warner’s assets, including HBO Max and CNN, with Paramount’s businesses, including CBS and Paramount+, as the companies work toward closing later this year, subject to regulatory review. Still, the approval was not a blank check. Shareholders separately rejected an advisory proposal on executive compensation tied to the merger, after scrutiny of a potential payout for Warner chief executive David Zaslav that one report said could reach as much as $887 million if the deal closes. Attention now turns to regulators, with reports saying authorities in Washington and London are expected to examine the merger’s effects before any final completion.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Pay protest: Proxy adviser ISS described Zaslav’s possible merger-linked payout as “extremely large,” and investors voted against the compensation plan even as they backed the deal itself.</li><li>Closing window: Warner said it expects the acquisition to close in the third fiscal quarter if regulators approve it, a sign that the companies are already planning for integration.</li><li>Political backdrop: The shareholder approval came as President Trump was due to attend a dinner with the Ellisons, billionaire backers of Paramount, according to the BBC.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Warner Bros Discovery shareholders: Investors overwhelmingly supported selling the company at $31 a share, signaling broad support for a larger combined media group despite unresolved regulatory reviews. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/warner-bros-shareholders-approve-paramount-merger/'>Michael West</a>)</li><li>Warner Bros Discovery investors on pay: Shareholders drew a clear line on executive rewards by rejecting the advisory compensation plan tied to the merger, even as they approved the sale itself. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/8934f738-fe99-4201-b190-a945d627bd9b'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Regulatory outlook: Reports say authorities in Washington and London are expected to scrutinize the merger’s impact, making competition and media-concentration concerns the next major hurdle for the companies. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/4/23/warner-bros-shareholders-approve-paramounts-takeover'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3351211/warner-bros-investors-back-us110-billion-merger-paramount-skydance'>Warner Bros investors back US$110 billion merger with Paramount Skydance</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/warner-bros-shareholders-approve-paramount-merger/'>Warner Bros shareholders approve Paramount merger</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/warner-bros-shareholders-approve-paramounts-81-billion-takeover-11399861#publisher=newsstand'>Warner Bros Shareholders Approve Paramount&#x27;s $81 Billion Takeover</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cgj09ny0dq6o'>Warner Bros shareholders approve Paramount&#x27;s $111bn takeover</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/8934f738-fe99-4201-b190-a945d627bd9b'>Warner Bros shareholders approve $111bn Paramount deal</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1stp22g/warner_bros_shareholders_approve_paramounts_81/'>Warner Bros shareholders approve Paramount&#x27;s $81 billion takeover | AP News</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/4/23/warner-bros-shareholders-approve-paramounts-takeover'>Warner Bros shareholders approve Paramount’s takeover</a> - aljaz